	<strings name="main_menu/settings_select/player_setup/player_profile_edit/video_settings/ray_tracing/help_strings">
		<string text=""/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="Ray tracing over Classic's light. Shadows: the sun's traced shadows and occlusion. Shadows + GI: also light bounced about the characters. All Lights: every light traced, kept to the level's brightness. For PRISM's own path tracing, choose Lighting PRISM Path Traced."/>
		<string text="The sun's shadows of vehicles, characters and weapons. Traced: ray traced, on the ground, on each other and on themselves. Classic's: the game's own, on the ground only."/>
		<string text="More rays a pixel: softer, steadier shadows and more of the bounced light, at more of the graphics card's time. Low suits the Steam Deck."/>
		<string text="Half traces a ray for each block of four pixels, cheaper on the graphics card; Full traces each pixel. Auto: full, but at Low quality."/>
		<string text="How the rays are smoothed: Full by their neighbours and the frames before, Temporal by the frames before alone, Off as they are."/>
		<string text="How far the bounced light may move a character's light from the game's own. CE keeps it; Full lets it go up to a quarter brighter or darker."/>
		<string text="All: the level's own sun shadows as sharp as the objects', every shadow as dark as the light rig says. Objects: only the objects' shadows traced."/>
		<string text="The level's shape the rays meet. Auto: the level as it is drawn, near and far. Far: the remodel's far level. Remodel: its near level, all of it. Game's: the map's own."/>
		<string text="How Classic's ray traced light looks: held to the game's lightmaps or lit by the traced lights alone, its lamps, exposure and highlights."/>
		<string text=""/>
		<string text="As Drawn: the replacement models' shapes where they are drawn, within 40 units (the game's own past that, and far objects left out when there are too many). Game's: the game's own models, cheaper."/>
		<string text="Keeps each object's traced shape from frame to frame, refitting only what moved: much less work. Off redoes them all each frame."/>
		<string text="Leaves, fences and grates cast shadows through their holes. With PRISM's lightings it is in the bake: a change bakes again."/>
	</strings>
</menus>
